---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro'
import AssertionCard from '../../components/AssertionCard.astro'
import ChartFigure from '../../components/ChartFigure.astro'
import { assertion } from '../../lib/feeds'
import { bar } from '../../lib/chart-spec'

const total = assertion('twenty-three-closings-in-twenty-two-years')
const villages = assertion('the-villages-outweigh-the-city')
const empty = assertion('ten-of-twenty-two-years-are-empty')
const cluster = assertion('two-years-carry-forty-four-per-cent')
const largest = assertion('the-largest-notice-is-not-a-factory-closing')

const twice = assertion('one-plant-appears-twice-under-two-owners')
const outside = assertion('nine-notices-gave-a-number-outside-ohio')

const shops = assertion('the-recession-produced-three-notices-and-all-were-shops')
const threshold = assertion('a-threshold-from-underneath')
const coincidence = assertion('two-thousand-six-hundred-and-twenty-four-against-two-thousand-six-hundred-and-twenty-eight')
const delphos = assertion('a-register-that-changes-its-mind-about-a-county')

const twelve = assertion('twelve-of-twenty-three-arrived-inside-sixty-days')
const zero = assertion('one-notice-arrived-on-the-day')
const ninety = assertion('only-three-notices-clear-ninety-days')
const timed = assertion('five-filings-timed-to-the-statute-and-eighteen-not')
const readings = assertion('the-file-dates-the-state-and-not-the-floor')
const rapid = assertion('rapid-response-had-under-sixty-days-half-the-time')

const named = assertion('thirteen-of-twenty-three-name-a-union')
const uaw = assertion('the-car-workers-union-in-a-county-with-no-car-plant')
const nobody = assertion('ten-notices-name-nobody-and-half-are-factories')
const column = assertion('the-union-column-takes-what-the-employer-wrote')
const after2011 = assertion('nothing-after-2011-names-a-union')

const years = Array.from({ length: 22 }, (_, i) => 1996 + i)
const workersByYear: Record<number, number> = {
  1996: 76, 1999: 204, 2001: 348, 2005: 246, 2006: 742, 2007: 417,
  2008: 80, 2009: 191, 2011: 153, 2012: 57, 2013: 104, 2016: 6,
}
const yearValues = years.map((y) => workersByYear[y] ?? 0)

const gaps: [string, number][] = [
  ['Superior Forge & Steel', 0],
  ["McDonald's Industrial Products", 12],
  ['Tower Automotive', 18],
  ['Experience Works', 25],
  ['Delphos Ohio Axle Plant', 35],
  ['Engineered Plastic Products', 37],
  ['Harvard Industries', 39],
  ['Spicer Driveshaft', 48],
  ['Lipari Foods', 51],
  ['Marathon Electric', 52],
  ['Grob Systems', 57],
  ['Mid Bus', 57],
  ['H & C Milcor', 60],
  ["Reser's Fine Foods", 60],
  ['Holland Binkley', 61],
  ['Spencerville Metal Systems', 61],
  ['Home Depot', 62],
  ['INEOS Nitriles', 68],
  ['The Andersons', 70],
  ['International Brake Industries', 81],
  ['Toledo Molding and Die', 94],
  ['Kmart Store #4301', 104],
  ['Continental Plastic Containers', 107],
]

const unions: [string, number][] = [
  ['UAW', 1049],
  ['no union named', 887],
  ['Iron Workers', 246],
  ['Steelworkers', 159],
  ['AFL-CIO', 109],
  ['PACE', 98],
  ['UPIU', 76],
]

const yearsSpec = bar(
  years.map(String),
  yearValues,
  { yTitle: 'Workers named in notices', labelValues: true },
)
const gapsSpec = bar(
  gaps.map(([n]) => n),
  gaps.map(([, d]) => d),
  { yTitle: 'Days from receipt to layoff', labelValues: true },
)
const unionsSpec = bar(
  unions.map(([n]) => n),
  unions.map(([, w]) => w),
  { yTitle: 'Workers named in notices', labelValues: true },
)
---

<Article slug="sixty-days-notice">
  <p>
    Allen County's industrial decline is well measured here and entirely anonymous. Manufacturing
    employment fell fifty-five per cent between 1986 and 2010; a fifth of the county's workplaces
    are gone; every job lost since 2001 was on somebody's payroll. Not one of those sentences names
    a plant, a date, or a person.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is a file that does. The Worker Adjustment and Retraining Notification Act obliges most
    employers of a hundred or more to give sixty days' notice of a plant closing or mass layoff, and
    Ohio published what it received, year by year, from 1996 to 2017. The state's own paths for it
    now answer 404 and its successor agency's hostname does not resolve; every file read here came
    out of the Internet Archive.
  </p>

  <h2>Twenty-three letters</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={total} open />
  <ChartFigure
    id="years"
    title="Workers named in Allen County layoff notices, by year"
    caption="Ten of the twenty-two years are empty. Two of them carry forty-four per cent of the record."
    columns={['Year', 'Workers']}
    rows={years.map((y, i) => [String(y), yearValues[i].toLocaleString()])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="years" set:html={JSON.stringify(yearsSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={villages} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={empty} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={cluster} />
  <p>
    2006 and 2007 are the two years the county lost its parts industry in public. Tower Automotive
    at Bluffton, Engineered Plastic Products and Marathon Electric at Lima, Spencerville Metal
    Systems, Toledo Molding and Die at Delphos — five plants making metal or plastic for somebody
    else's assembly line, inside twenty months.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={largest} />

  <h2>One plant, twice</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={twice} open />
  <p>
    The register has no identifier for a place of work: no address, no facility number, nothing that
    would let two notices seven years apart be recognised as the same building. What joins them is
    the telephone number, which nobody put in the file for that purpose. The plant that let a
    hundred and four people go in 1999 let two hundred and thirteen go in 2006 under a different
    company's name.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={outside} />

  <h2>What the register cannot see</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={shops} open />
  <AssertionCard assertion={threshold} />
  <p>
    That is the most useful thing this file does, and it does it by being empty. The Act has
    thresholds — a hundred employees, fifty affected at one site, sixty days — and a decline made of
    twenty people here and thirty there passes under all of them without leaving a line. The
    steepest fall in the modern part of the county's manufacturing series happened with nobody
    required to announce anything.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={coincidence} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={delphos} />

  <h2>Sixty days</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={twelve} open />
  <ChartFigure
    id="intervals"
    title="Days between the state's receipt of the notice and the layoff"
    caption="Twelve of the twenty-three fall short of the sixty the Act names. Two sit exactly on it and three more within two days; the rest are scattered."
    columns={['Employer', 'Days']}
    rows={gaps.map(([n, d]) => [n, d])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="intervals" set:html={JSON.stringify(gapsSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={zero} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={ninety} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={timed} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={readings} />
  <p>
    So the number is published and the conclusion is not. The Act's sixty days run to the workers,
    to any representative of theirs, and to the state; the register dates the third of those and
    nothing else. A row at nought days is a documented fact about what Columbus knew and when, and
    it is not proof that anybody on the floor was surprised.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={rapid} />

  <h2>Who was in the room</h2>
  <p>
    The register carries a column headed <em>Union</em>, which makes it the only source assembled
    here that says whether a particular workplace in this county was organised.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={named} open />
  <ChartFigure
    id="unions"
    title="Workers by the union named on the notice"
    caption="Thirteen notices name a union and ten name nobody. The federation row, AFL-CIO, identifies no bargaining unit at all."
    columns={['Named', 'Workers']}
    rows={unions.map(([n, w]) => [n, w.toLocaleString()])}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="unions" set:html={JSON.stringify(unionsSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={uaw} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={nobody} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={column} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={after2011} />
  <p>
    The last union in the county's closing register is UAW Local 975, at International Brake
    Industries in Lima, in March 2011. After it: a food distributor, a food plant and a federal
    employment programme for older workers, and in the union column of all three, nothing.
  </p>
</Article>
